export anchor VintageTravelPosterStyle:
    number: 140
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Vintage travel poster
    idea: A 1930s railway poster wall, where the greeting sits under a sunlit flat landscape and each project is a little poster whose sun rises as its tasks are done.
    base: light
    palette:
        wall: #efe3c8, the page and field fill
        cream: #fbf3e0, poster mounts, bands and cards
        navy: #1f2f4a, text, frames and the primary button
        slate: #55607a, captions and meta
        sun: #f6c453, suns and the focus halo, never text
        apricot: #f2a65a, sky gradients and last week bars
        rose: #d9675a, far hills and the nav underline
        teal: #2b6f6b, middle hills and this week bars
        sea: #1d4e5f, near hills and cypress trees
        pineText: #22625e, the On track star
        ochre: #8a4f00, the At risk half sun
        terracotta: #a63d22, the Behind cloud and overdue stamp
    type:
        Display uses Futura, Century Gothic, Avenir Next, Gill Sans in bold
        caps tracked 0.08 to 0.3em. Condensed lettering uses Futura
        Condensed, Avenir Next Condensed, Arial Narrow at 800. Body uses
        Optima, Candara, Segoe UI. Destination lettering up to 120px,
        numbers 46px condensed, greeting 32px caps, poster titles 15px caps,
        body 16px at 1.55, captions 11px caps tracked 0.24em.
    layout:
        A cream header with the spaced brand, an underlined search, a navy
        New project, a round bell and the user name in caps, over centred
        spaced caps nav with a rose underline, closed by a double rule. The
        hero is a mounted poster with a flat sunset scene of hills, cypress
        and a sailboat under huge Brightwork lettering, and a cream band
        with the date, greeting and a tilted overdue stamp. Four mounted
        tickets carry flat icons and the numbers. Six portrait mini posters
        show a gradient sky, a percent, a sun whose height follows progress
        and hills, then name, category, tasks, due and status. Below are a
        Travel diary and an Itinerary bar chart with sunset bars for last
        week and sea bars for this week.
    spacing: An 8px unit. Cream mounts 8 to 12px wide, 18 to 28px gaps, 44px between sections.
    density: Low. A big hero poster, four tickets, six small posters.
    corners: Square everywhere, only suns and the bell are round.
    borders: A 2px navy frame inside a cream mount, double rules under the header and above the sheet.
    shadows: Soft hung on a wall drops, 0 8px 18px navy at 15 to 20 percent.
    icons: Flat filled shapes. Four point star On track, half sun on the horizon At risk, cloud Behind, ringed exclamation stamp for overdue.
    focus: A 3px navy outline offset 3px inside an 8px sun halo.
    tone: Travel copy in spaced caps, such as Visit the week ahead, Destinations, Travel diary and Itinerary.
